<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hagia Sophia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">537 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hagia Sophia is a great domed church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> completed in 537 CE under the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a>. For centuries it was the cathedral of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and one of the largest buildings in the world. After the Ottoman conquest of the city in 1453 it was converted into a mosque.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia.jpg" alt="Hagia Sophia" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adli Wahid · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hagia_Sophia_(228968325).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
